why_this_one:
It is the whole of the client's Ice, in ZzzCharacter.cpp's damage arm:

    case AT_SKILL_ICE:
        CreateEffect(MODEL_ICE, to->Position, o->Angle, Light);
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
            CreateEffect(MODEL_ICE_SMALL, to->Position, o->Angle, o->Light);
        if (c->SkillSuccess) g_CharacterRegisterBuff(to, eDeBuff_Freeze);
        PlayBuffer(SOUND_ICE);
        break;

One block, five shards, one wave and a debuff icon. Note the two lights: the block is given the local `Light` the damage arm computed and the shards the caster's own `o->Light`.

Note also whose angle. Both are created with `o->Angle` - the *caster's* facing, not the target's - so the block is oriented to the man who threw it and a monster spun round inside it is spun inside a block that did not turn. That is MU's, and it is the kind of thing that reads as a bug in a screenshot taken from the wrong side.
